## Build Array from Permutation

##Approach
-- Create a new array ans with the same length as nums.
-- Traverse through every index i using a for loop.
-- For each index, first find nums[i].
-- Use that value as another index to get nums[nums[i]].
-- Store the result in ans[i].
-- After processing all indices, return the ans array.

## Time Complexity
O(n) — We traverse the array once.
## Space Complexity
O(n) — We create a new array ans of size n.

SOULTION : 
public int[] buildArray(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] newArr = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            newArr[i] = nums[nums[i]];
        }
        return newArr;

    }
